# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECURITY — Netlify & Git (read before deploy)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# • Do not commit a real `.env` — only this `.env.example` (placeholders) belongs in git.
# • Production: add values in Netlify → Site configuration → Environment variables
#   (encrypted at rest; not visible in the public repo). EmailJS variables below MUST use
#   the VITE_ prefix and MUST exist before `npm run build` — add them in Netlify, then click
#   “Deploy site” again. If the form says the online form is not active, the build did not
#   see these three: VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY, VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID, VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID.
# • Variables prefixed with VITE_ are compiled into the browser bundle — anyone can
#   read them in deployed JS. Use VITE_* only for EmailJS public key / template &
#   service IDs (required for the browser SDK) and non-secret toggles like
#   VITE_WHATSAPP_NOTIFY_ENABLED.
# • Keep truly secret values server-side only (no VITE_ prefix): WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN,
#   WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID, CONTACT_NOTIFY_SECRET, GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY, GOOGLE_PLACE_ID.
# • Optional: run `npm run deploy:check` locally before push — fails if `.env` is
#   accidentally tracked by git.
#
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# EmailJS — https://dashboard.emailjs.com/
#
# ── Why you might not see “Service ID” ──────────────────────────────────────
# EmailJS does not give you a Service ID until you connect at least ONE mail
# provider (Gmail, Outlook, etc.). That connection is called an “Email Service”.
#
# Steps:
#   1. Open: https://dashboard.emailjs.com/admin  (menu: Email Services)
#   2. Click “Add New Service” and pick Gmail (or another provider).
#   3. Finish linking / OAuth for your inbox (e.g. adv.ipnathan@gmail.com).
#   4. Back on the Email Services list, click your new service — the Service ID
#      is shown there (short id like `service_xxxx` or `gmail` etc.).
#   5. Create an Email Template under “Email Templates”; copy its Template ID.
#   6. Public Key: Account → General (or API Keys) — labeled “Public Key”.
#
# If you set ONE service as the account default in the dashboard, EmailJS allows
# the reserved id below instead of pasting the full Service ID:
#
#   VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=default_service
#
# Template variables used by this app are listed at the bottom.

VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=

# Optional: inbox that receives enquiries (defaults to FIRM_EMAIL in code). Use if the template expects it elsewhere.
# VITE_EMAILJS_INBOX_EMAIL=adv.ipnathan@gmail.com

# If your template “To Email” uses a custom variable (e.g. {{company_email}}), set the param name here:
# VITE_EMAILJS_TO_TEMPLATE_PARAM=company_email

# Second template — acknowledgement to the customer (required for two-email flow).
# Create a separate template and paste its ID here. “To Email” must be {{to_email}} (the visitor).
VITE_EMAILJS_AUTOREPLY_TEMPLATE_ID=

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# TEMPLATE 1 — TO YOUR INBOX (VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# To Email:    your firm address OR {{to_email}}
# From Name:   {{from_name}}   (or “Website enquiry”)
# Reply To:    {{reply_to}}
# Subject:     {{subject}}     → e.g. “New website enquiry — Serious offences & Sessions trials”
#
# Content (example):
#   New enquiry from your website
#
#   Name:        {{from_name}}
#   Email:       {{from_email}}
#   Phone:       {{phone}}
#   Matter type: {{matter_type}}
#
#   Message / details (brief description only — name/email/phone/matter are separate variables above):
#   {{inquiry_body}}
#
# Variables always sent: {{title}} (same as matter type), {{subject}}, {{matter_type}},
# {{from_name}}, {{from_email}}, {{reply_to}}, {{phone}}, {{inquiry_body}}, {{message}}, {{time}},
# plus compatibility keys documented previously.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# TEMPLATE 2 — ACKNOWLEDGEMENT TO CUSTOMER (VITE_EMAILJS_AUTOREPLY_TEMPLATE_ID)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# To Email:    {{to_email}}     ← visitor’s address (required)
# From Name:   M.P. Law Firm   (or your firm name)
# Subject:     Thank you for contacting M.P. Law Firm
#
# Content (paste and adjust):
#   Hi {{name}},
#
#   Thank you for reaching out to us! We have received your request: "{{title}}", and we'll get back to you shortly.
#
#   Best regards,
#   The M.P. Law Firm Team
#
# Variables sent: {{name}}, {{title}} (matter type label), {{to_email}},
# optional {{message}} / {{acknowledgement}} (full legacy body in site language).

# ── Troubleshooting ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# “The recipients address is empty”: set “To Email” on each template as above — not blank.
# For template 1, do not use {{email}} as the firm inbox; use a literal address or {{to_email}}.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# WhatsApp Business — Meta Cloud API (optional firm notifications)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Sends the same enquiry summary as a WhatsApp message after EmailJS succeeds.
# Tokens MUST stay server-side — only configure these on Netlify / backend (never commit real values).
#
# Setup overview:
#   1. Meta Business → WhatsApp → API Setup: create / select app, get a permanent access token.
#   2. Note “Phone number ID” (WhatsApp → API Setup), not the display phone number.
#   3. WHATSAPP_NOTIFY_TO = recipient in digits only, country code included, no + (e.g. 919940717742).
#      Use the number that should receive enquiry alerts (often your business mobile).
#
# Production note: Meta may require an approved *template* for business-initiated chats outside
# the 24-hour customer-service window. Session messages work best after the customer has messaged
# your WhatsApp Business number. See Meta’s WhatsApp Cloud API docs for your account tier.

# Client: set true only when server env below is configured on Netlify.
# VITE_WHATSAPP_NOTIFY_ENABLED=true

# Optional shared secret so only your site can call the function (set same value in Netlify):
# VITE_CONTACT_NOTIFY_SECRET=your-long-random-string
# CONTACT_NOTIFY_SECRET=your-long-random-string

# Server-only (Netlify environment variables — not VITE_*):
# WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
# WHATSAPP_NOTIFY_TO=
